invariant: INV-16
file: poly1305_ifma.c
catches: poly1305_equiv_test
reason: the carry adds t2's bits from 42 up to digit 0 once rather than
  5 times, so every group loses the part of its sums at 2^130 and above
  that is 5 modulo 2^130 - 5, and the tag is wrong for every update the
  kernel takes. bin/poly1305_equiv_test runs the kernel's own text over
  the lane model on every host and compares it with poly1305.c's loop.

--- old
    h[0] = lanes_add(lanes_and(t0, mask), lanes_times_5(lanes_shift_right(t2, 42)));
--- new
    h[0] = lanes_add(lanes_and(t0, mask), lanes_shift_right(t2, 42));
